<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 382 0 R
/E (KNN relies on distance measurements between points, which become unreliable as dimensions increase, with 25 features and only 284 training points, the unusually high k=20 reflects this compensation, averaging over more neighbours to stabilise noisy distance estimates. The Decision Tree is unaffected as it splits purely on information gain at each node, making dimensionality irrelevant to its performance. Applying PCA prior to KNN to reduce dimensionality could make distance estimates more reliable and improve recall further.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
